Thanks, here's one for the divers :)
I've managed a few dives for the castle where I start an elven wizard,
find a pick-axe and maybe even sac for MagicBane and then dive to the
castle.  Sometimes I make it, mostly I don't.  But the problem I see
IME is that even with a guaranteed 'Elbereth' and a drawbridge
instrument, the Medusa level with the titan is very difficult, and if
a summoning storm occurs there or at the castle, with say a captain an
umber hulk and/or a minotaur things go really bad.  So even if I pass
all of that I still need to streak with an AC somewhere between 5 and
9 through the throneroom monsters to the castle wand so that I can
wish for armor.  I probably need more practice and perhaps even in a
diving situation I need to temper things.  With my last character, who
ascended, I made it the castle at 9000 turns but then I was vulnerable
to one-hit kills so I felt that I had to spend several thousand turns
trying to lead monsters back to the drawbridge.

